Evidence: Document.pm:32 decodes leniently (`slurp_utf8`), set_paragraph writes the whole document back (:99). A Latin-1 page "# Caf\xE9\ncr\xE8me\n## Other\nna\xEFve\n" after update_paragraph on section Other: every non-ASCII byte in the file became EF BF BD; the tool reported success.

Fix (main agent's call, the smallest change that stops the data loss): writes (update_paragraph, restore_section) to a page whose bytes are not valid UTF-8 are refused with an error naming the page and the reason; the file stays byte-identical. Reads keep today's lenient behavior.

Tests: Latin-1 page: update refused, isError, bytes unchanged; a valid UTF-8 page with umlauts, CJK and emoji still round-trips through get_paragraph/update_paragraph.

tests: t/23-document-encoding.t (Latin-1 page: update_paragraph and restore_section via stand-in must give isError mentioning UTF-8 + page, bytes unchanged, no restore event; reads still answer; valid UTF-8 umlaut/CJK/emoji page round-trips byte-identically and a real edit changes only the target section). Red on HEAD: the two refusal subtests (isError false, bytes corrupted); read and UTF-8 subtests pass today as guards.

Test bug in t/23 (TB): line 82 calls JSON::MaybeXS::decode_json on $got->{content}[0]{text}, which MCP::Tool::structured_result builds with Mojo to_json as a CHARACTER string -> 'Wide character in subroutine entry', script dies after subtest 4's first check (exit 255, no plan) on HEAD and now alike. Fix: JSON::MaybeXS->new( utf8 => 0 )->decode(...) or read $got->{structuredContent}{content}. With that one-line change in a /tmp copy: HEAD Document+Server -> subtests 1,2 red, 3,4 green; new -> 4/4 green. Also stale now: core skill line 143 says restore writes via _resolve_page($page)->spew_utf8; it now reads via $doc->read_for_update and writes via $doc->write_text (skill is not in my lane).

Done (code). Document.pm: one raw read (_slurp: slurp_raw; valid = utf8::decode ok and no surrogates / code points above U+10FFFF, noncharacters allowed; otherwise lenient Encode decode with U+FFFD). New public read_for_update -> (LF text, eol), croaks 'Page <name relative to wiki_root> is not valid UTF-8: refusing to write it, which would replace its invalid bytes with U+FFFD'; new public write_text($text, $eol) = LF->eol, utf8::encode (exact inverse of the decode), spew_raw - the single write place for k15. set_paragraph uses both; get_toc/get_paragraph/content stay lenient (content now decodes via _slurp, POD added). Server.pm restore_section closure only: reads via $doc->read_for_update (refusal before History is called), passes the LF text as current_content, writes History's result via $doc->write_text($result->{content}, $eol). Verified: t/23 1-3 green in tree (4 needs TB's line-82 fix, see note; 4/4 green with it, 1-2 red on HEAD); t/20/21/22 green. Differential vs HEAD Document over 10 fixtures (LF/CRLF umlaut+CJK+emoji, BOM, U+FFFF/U+FDD0 noncharacters, literal U+FFFD, NUL, ASCII, empty, Latin-1 LF/CRLF): content, TOC, every get_paragraph, round trips and set_paragraph bytes identical, except Latin-1 pages: HEAD wrote EF BF BD (corruption), now refused with bytes identical; reads no longer print Unicode::UTF8's 'Can't decode' warnings. Restore via stand-in: LF page same as HEAD; CRLF page gets LF current_content and is written back CRLF; Latin-1 page: isError, History not called, bytes identical. prove -lr t/: no new failures - every red file (t/24, 39, 43-48) fails the same tests with HEAD's Document+Server (t/45 43/61 differ only by the absolute -I path of the comparison run).

